In
http://users.digitalkingdom.org/~rlpowell/hobbies/lojban/grammar/lojban.peg=
.txt
(where can I find the file used by camxes?)
There is this rule

term-1 <- sumti / ( !gek (tag / FA-clause free*) (sumti / KU-clause? free*)
) / termset / NA-clause KU-clause free*


I don't have a firm grasp of formal grammars, so correct me if I am wrong.

1. This rule is relevant.
2. If we make the KU-clause mandatory, instead of optional, my mental
grammar is realized.

term-1 <- sumti / ( !gek (tag / FA-clause free*) (sumti / KU-clause free*)
) / termset / NA-clause KU-clause free*

3. It would contradict the CLL, though. http://dag.github.io/cll/9/9/

Fact is I didn't internalize the elidability of {ku} in this case. I still
don't like it...

mu'o
mi'e .asiz.




